-- The SPH + SG48100P commissioning map now renders on /calculators/system.
--
-- Six ProtectionOutput rows, generator kW as an optional input, and work mode
-- kept out of the protection register. Status is already in_development; this
-- moves the percent and rewrites the description, whose "Remaining" line still
-- named the map as unbuilt.
--
-- Keep in sync with supabase/seed.sql (CI enforces this).

update public.roadmap_items
  set dev_percent_complete = 45,
      description = 'Started 2026-09-03; the map itself landed 2026-09-04. BATTERY_PRESETS admitted the SG48100P from the manufacturer''s own manual (Shopify CDN, linked from sungoldpower.com/pages/user-manual), with seriesCount 16 derived from 51.2 V LiFePO4, recommended charge 54.5 V kept DISTINCT from the SPH L16 boost of 56.8 V, and battery-preset-review.ts catching a 15S slip and an L16 voltage copied onto the battery row. The battery step publishes presetId when that pack is picked; chemistry alone remains the normal path, and summaries saved before this field existed simply have no id. The inverter step publishes the matching INVERTER_PRESETS id the same way. The map now renders on /calculators/system for an SPH8048P or SPH10048P against an SG48100P: six ProtectionOutput rows (item 08 battery type as L16 with the GEL factory default in the derivation, items 32/33 CAN + SGP with the BMS icon as the confirmation, charge voltage carrying 54.5 V and 56.8 V side by side without picking one, items 59/60 as percent remaining and only after comms, item 16 equalize DIS, and the charge-current ceilings), generator kW as an optional input that prints "not given" rather than inventing an amp, and work mode listed as a use-case choice outside the protection register. An admitted SPH chosen without the SG48100P is told which pack to pick rather than shown a partial map. Remaining: cable ampacity as the fourth charge-current ceiling -- the protection step publishes its sized runs but the map does not read them yet; the generator''s ATS and the dry-contact auto-start in SPH manual 6.5; and item 03 UPS vs APL, which these PDFs do not answer. The Install step the sizing chain does not have. Step 7 currently reads disagreements between calculators; it never tells someone with a chosen SPH10048P and SG48100P which LCD item to change, so they leave the factory GEL profile on a lithium pack. That is differentiator #1 inverted: the manuals are in pdf/ and already cited by INVERTER_PRESETS and PANEL_PRESETS, and the user still has to be the one who speaks both. NOT a cheat sheet and not a new calculator. A mapping, gated on admitted equipment IDs, rendered on /calculators/system through ProtectionOutput. Each row is a ProtectionView: the inverter menu item, the set of options that pass, the arithmetic, and both manuals cited. Never a single "set Program 09 to 56.8 V." "Recommended" is rejected by assertProtectionView, same as the rest of the protection register. WHY THIS IS PROTECTION, NOT CAPACITY. Wrong charge voltage, wrong battery type, equalize left on, or a generator charge current above what the machine can supply, destroy equipment or stall a generator. The existing cutoff-voltage output already classified the stop-using-the-battery half; this item is the rest of that menu, equipment-specific. Work mode (UTI/SBU/SOL/SUB) is a use-case choice and stays out of the protection register -- the map asks which job the system has, it does not pick one. THE FAILURE THIS EXISTS TO PREVENT is picking a side of a datasheet conflict and putting the site''s authority behind it. Same brand, same three PDFs: the SG48100P sheet says charge at 54.5 V and stay in 20-95% SOC; the SPH L16 preset charges at 56.8 V; the inverter ships as GEL. The map must surface that disagreement the way system-design.ts surfaces the odd-panel-count mismatch, not resolve it. Lithium stop-using-the-battery is percent remaining after BMS comms (items 32/33 SGP, then 59/60/61), matching cutoffProtectionView. If comms are not confirmed, the option is "establish comms", not a voltage. GENERATOR IS AN INPUT, NOT A PV SETTING. The panel datasheet is already consumed by the array step (Voc vs 500 V, MPPT 125-425 V). Generator lives on AC-in plus the dry-contact auto-start in SPH manual 6.5, and needs the generator''s kW and whether it has ATS. Charge current is min(battery max x parallel count, inverter item 07/28, generator leftover after loads, cable ampacity). Missing any of those four, do not emit amps -- show the missing question. Item 03 UPS vs APL is generator-quality, also unanswered by these PDFs. V1 SCOPE is one admitted pairing: SPH8048P or SPH10048P + SG48100P, when those preset IDs are the ones chosen. Typed-in-by-hand specs, or an EG4 inverter against a Sun Gold battery, get the generic inverter-settings guide, not a map -- menu IDs are firmware-and-model-specific and a wrong ID is worse than none. The SG550WM does not appear on the map; its job is the array step. DATA SHAPE. battery_models cannot carry this: it has dod_rated and chemistry, not charge voltage, series count (16S), BMS protocol, or max charge current. Admit a BATTERY_PRESETS row (sibling of INVERTER_PRESETS) from the manufacturer''s own manual, with commissioning-review.ts catching transcription errors (voltage order 15<12<04<14<35<37<05<09, L16 is 16S not 15S, equalize off for LFP, GEL-default trap present). Every menu mapping cites manual + page. Tests lock the SPH L16 and SG48100P numbers to those pages so a later cleanup cannot silently pick 56.8. TRACK 1 IS NOT TRACK 2. The neighbor''s actual settings belong in neighbor-build/, dated to a firmware version. The public map generates the same derivation for anyone who selected this pairing. Do not paste the neighbor''s numbers into the product. Depends on the spec library admission gate and the protection-register chrome; it does not absorb either. The licensed-electrician sign-off, clickwrap, and professional-review items stay independent gates -- a bigger disclaimer is not a substitute, and showing the derivation of a WRONG number documents the error. Phase 1 rather than phase 0 because the product currently omits this output rather than emitting a wrong one. First phase-1 item to pick up after the spec library can admit a battery programming row.'
  where title = 'System designer: commissioning map for chosen equipment';
